 [in LXX for בַּיִת, פָּנִים and cognate forms ;] \n__1. from within: Mrk.7:21, 23, Luk.11:7. \n __2. within: Mat.7:15 23:25-28, 2Co.7:5, Rev.4:8 5:1; τὸ ἔ., Luk.11:40; id. with genitive, Luk.11:39.†\n (AS)","source_line":2223}],"occurrence_count":12,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"dentro","count":9},{"gloss":"interior","count":2},{"gloss":"por-dentro","count":1}]},"G2217":{"id":"G2217","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2217","disambiguated_id":"G2217 =","unique_id":"G2217","headword":"ζόφος","transliteration":"zophos","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"darkness","definition_en":"ζόφος, -ου, ὁ\n (akin to γνόφος, which see), [in Sm.: Exo.10:22, Job.28:3, Psa.11:2 91:6, Isa.59:9 * ;] \nin Hom, the gloom of the under-world; hence, darkness, deep gloom (poët. and late prose writers): Heb.12:18, 2Pe.2:4 2:17, Ju 6 13.†\n ὁμίχλη, -ης, ἡ, \n [in LXX for עֲרָפֶל, etc. ;] \na mist: 2Pe.2:17 \n SYN.: νέφος, νεφέλη, both thicker than ὁ (AS)","source_line":2362}],"occurrence_count":5,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"escuridão","count":5}]},"G2369":{"id":"G2369","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2369","disambiguated_id":"G2369 =","unique_id":"G2369","headword":"θυμιατήριον","transliteration":"thumiatērion","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"incense altar","definition_en":"θυμιατήριον, -ου, τό\n (θυμιάω), [in LXX: 2Ch.26:19, Eze.8:11 (קְטֹרֶת), 4Ma.7:11 * ;] \n__1. as in cl. (Hdt., iv, 162; Thuc., vi, 46) and LXX, a censer: Heb.9:4 (but see infr., and cf. Westc., in l). \n __2. As in Philo., rer. div., § 46, FlJ, Ant., iv, 2, 4, al., the altar of incense: He, l.with (but see supr. and cf. MM, Exp., xv).†\n (AS)","source_line":2518}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"incensário","count":1}]},"G2503":{"id":"G2503","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2503","disambiguated_id":"G2503 =","unique_id":"G2503","headword":"ἰῶτα","transliteration":"iōta","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"iota","definition_en":"ἰῶτα, τό ,\n iota (Heb. י, i.e. the smallest letter): Mat.5:18.†\n (AS)","source_line":2684}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"passem","count":1}]},"G2758":{"id":"G2758","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2758","disambiguated_id":"G2758 =","unique_id":"G2758","headword":"κενόω","transliteration":"kenoō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to empty","definition_en":"κενόω, -ῶ \n (κενός, which see), [in LXX: Jer.14:2 15:9 (עָמָל pu.)* ;] \nto empty. Metaphorical, to empty, make empty, vain or of no effect: καύχημα, 1Co.9:15; ἑαυτόν, of Christ, Php.2:7 (v Lft.; ICC, in 1, and esp. Gifford, Incarn., 54 ff.); pass., πίστις, Rom.4:14; ὁ σταυρός, 1Co.1:17; καύχημα, 2Co.9:3†\n (AS)","source_line":2948}],"occurrence_count":5,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"logo","count":3},{"gloss":"assunto","count":2}]},"G2924":{"id":"G2924","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2924","disambiguated_id":"G2924 =","unique_id":"G2924","headword":"κριτικός","transliteration":"kritikos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"discerning","definition_en":"κριτικός, -ή, -όν\n (κρίνω), \ncritical, able to discern or judge: with genitive obj., Heb.4:12.†\n (AS)","source_line":3119}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"apta","count":1}]},"G3509":{"id":"G3509","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3509","disambiguated_id":"G3509 =","unique_id":"G3509","headword":"νέφος","transliteration":"nephos","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"cloud","definition_en":"νέφος, -ους, τό \n [in LXX for עָב, שַׁחַק, עָנַן ;] \na mass of clouds, a cloud (cf. νεφέλη); metaphorically as in Hom., Hdt., al.), of a dense throng: Heb.12:1.†\n (AS)","source_line":3622}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"nuvem","count":1}]},"G3625":{"id":"G3625","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3625","disambiguated_id":"G3625 =","unique_id":"G3625","headword":"οἰκουμένη","transliteration":"oikoumenē","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"world","definition_en":"οἰκουμένη, -ης, ἡ\n (fern. Pres. pass. ptcp. of οἰκέω; sc. γῆ) [in LXX chiefly for תֵּבֵל, אֶרֶץ ;] \nthe inhabited earth; \n __(a) in cl., the countries occupied by Greeks, as disting. from barbarian lands (Hdt., Dem., al.); \n __(b) in later writers, the Roman world: Luk.2:1, Act.11:28 24:5; by meton., of its inhabitants : Act.17:6 19:27; \n __(with) in LXX (Psa.23:1 71:8, al.) and NT, also of the whole inhabited world: Mat.24:14, Luk.4:5 21:26, Rom.10:18, Heb.1:6, Rev.3:10 16:14; by meton. (ut supr.), Act.17:31, Rev.12:9; \n __(d) of the Messianic age, ἡ οἰ. ἡ μέλλουσα = ὁ αἰὼ ὁ μέλλων: Heb.2:5.†\n (AS)","source_line":3741}],"occurrence_count":15,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"mundo","count":13},{"gloss":"terra","count":2}]},"G3650":{"id":"G3650","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3650","disambiguated_id":"G3650 =","unique_id":"G3650","headword":"ὅλος","transliteration":"holos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"all","definition_en":"ὅλος, -η, -ον, \n [in LXX chiefly for כֹּל ;] \nof persons and things, whole, entire, complete; \n__1. of indefinite ideas, with subst. anarth.: Luk.5:5, Act.11:26 28:30, Tit.1:11; ὅλον ἄνθρωπον (an entire man; see Field, Notes, 93), Jhn.7:23; ὅλη Ἰερουσαλήμ (= πᾶσα Ἰ, Mat.2:3; see Bl., §47, 9), Act.21:31. \n __2. Definite, with art.; \n__(a) preceding subst.: Mat.4:23, 24 Luk.8:39, 1Co.12:17, al.; \n __(b) following subst.: Mrk.1:33, Luk.9:25, Jhn.4:53, Act.21:30, al.; \n __(with) between art. and subst., where subst. is an abstract noun (Plat., al.). \n __3. Attached to adj. or verb: Mat.13:33, Luk.13:21, Jhn.9:34, al.; adverbially, δι ̓ ὅλου (MM, xviii), Jhn.19:23. \n (AS)","source_line":3766}],"occurrence_count":108,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"toda","count":53},{"gloss":"todo","count":44},{"gloss":"todas","count":3},{"gloss":"tudo","count":2},{"gloss":"completo","count":2},{"gloss":"tudo-fermentado","count":1},{"gloss":"tudo-levedado","count":1},{"gloss":"inteiros","count":1},{"gloss":"inteiras","count":1}]},"G3675":{"id":"G3675","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3675","disambiguated_id":"G3675 =","unique_id":"G3675","headword":"ὁμόφρων","transliteration":"homophrōn","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"like-minded","definition_en":"ὁμόφρων, -ον\n (ὁμός, φρήν), = ὁμόνοος, \nagreeing, of one mind: 1Pe.3:8.†\n (AS)","source_line":3791}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"de-mesmo-sentimento","count":1}]},"G3696":{"id":"G3696","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3696","disambiguated_id":"G3696 =","unique_id":"G3696","headword":"ὅπλον","transliteration":"hoplon","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"weapon","definition_en":"ὅπλον, -ου, τό \n [in LXX for מָגֵן, צִנָּה, etc. ;] \n__1. a tool, implement, instrument: ὅπλα ἀδικίας (Opp. to ὅ. δικαιοσύνης), Rom.6:13. \n __2. Freq., in pl., arms, weapons: Jhn.18:3, 2Co.10:4; metaphorically, τ. φωτός, Rom.13:12; τ. δικαιοσύνης, 2Co.6:7.†\n (AS)","source_line":3812}],"occurrence_count":6,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"armas","count":4},{"gloss":"instrumentos","count":2}]},"G3892":{"id":"G3892","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3892","disambiguated_id":"G3892 =","unique_id":"G3892","headword":"παρανομία","transliteration":"paranomia","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"lawlessness","definition_en":"παρανομία, -ας, ἡ \n [in LXX: Psa.37:7 (מְזִמָּה), etc. ;] \nlaw-breaking, transgression: 2Pe.2:16.†\n (AS)","source_line":4010}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"transgressão","count":1}]},"G423":{"id":"G423","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0423","disambiguated_id":"G0423 =","unique_id":"G0423","headword":"ἀνεπίληπτος","transliteration":"anepilēptos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"irreproachable","definition_en":"ἀν-επί-λημπτος (Rec. -λμπτος; Bl., § 6, 8), -ον \n (ἀ- ἐπιλαμβάνω) \nwithout reproach: 1Ti.3:2 5:7 6:14.†\n SYN.: ἀμεμπτος, ἀνέγκλητος. It is stronger than these, for it implies not only that the man is of good report, but that he is deservedly so (cf. MM, VGT, see word). (AS)","source_line":529}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"irrepreensível","count":2},{"gloss":"irrepreensíveis","count":1}]},"G435":{"id":"G435","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0435","disambiguated_id":"G0435G =","unique_id":"G0435G","headword":"ἀνήρ","transliteration":"anēr","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"man","definition_en":"ἀνήρ, ἀνδρός, ὁ, \n [in LXX chiefly for אִישׁ, frequently אֱנוֹשׁ, also אָדָם, etc. ;] \na man, Lat. vir. \n__1. As opposite to a woman, Act.8:12, 1Ti.2:12; as a husband, Mat.1:16, Jhn.4:16, Rom.7:2, Tit.1:6. \n __2. As opposite to a boy or infant, 1Co.13:11, Eph.4:13, Jas.3:2. \n __3. In appos. with a noun or adj., as ἀ. ἁμαρτωλός, Luk.5:8; ἀ. προφήτης, 24:19; frequently in terms of address, as ἀ. ἀδελφοί, Act.1:16; and esp. with gentilic names, as ἀ. Ἰουδαῖος, Act.22:3; ἀ. Ἐφέσιοι, 19:35. \n __4. In general, a man, a male person: = τις, Luk.8:41, Act.6:11. \n SYN.: ἄνθρωπος, which see (cf. MM, VGT, see word). (AS)","source_line":541},{"source_id":"G0435","disambiguated_id":"G0435H = a Meaning of","unique_id":"G0435G","headword":"ἀνήρ","transliteration":"anēr","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"man: husband","definition_en":"ἀνήρ, ἀνδρός, ὁ, \n [in LXX chiefly for אִישׁ, frequently אֱנוֹשׁ, also אָדָם, etc. ;] \na man, Lat. vir. \n__1. As opposite to a woman, Act.8:12, 1Ti.2:12; as a husband, Mat.1:16, Jhn.4:16, Rom.7:2, Tit.1:6. \n __2. As opposite to a boy or infant, 1Co.13:11, Eph.4:13, Jas.3:2. \n __3. In appos. with a noun or adj., as ἀ. ἁμαρτωλός, Luk.5:8; ἀ. προφήτης, 24:19; frequently in terms of address, as ἀ. ἀδελφοί, Act.1:16; and esp. with gentilic names, as ἀ. Ἰουδαῖος, Act.22:3; ἀ. Ἐφέσιοι, 19:35. \n __4. In general, a man, a male person: = τις, Luk.8:41, Act.6:11. \n SYN.: ἄνθρωπος, which see (cf. MM, VGT, see word). (AS)","source_line":542}]